// result_end
\caption(Complete same-grid width studies with actual tap counts and explicit baselines.)
\alttext(Measured finite-grid errors distinguish raw and normalized windows; the tap count is actual selected work, not elapsed time or a universal accuracy bound.)

> Scope and verification

Complete finite nonempty samples, positive lobes, finite queries and
representable integer window geometry are checked before indexing or copies.
Query clamping precedes floor-to-integer conversion. Every product/sum/result
must remain finite; this conservative arithmetic policy can reject data whose
ideal cancellation would be finite. Scalar queries cost O(n+a) including
validation; vector queries validate once and cost O(n+Q*a). Trace admission
counts all n original samples plus2*a actual tap records before
copies/evaluation, with a million-entry default and zero disabling only that
optional cap. It excludes fields/capacities/bytes/RAM. All records own their
values and no replay constructs taps.

Independent scalar sinc/weight references verified2000 resamplings and11892
actual tap records, including raw versus normalized accumulation and clamped
lookup identities. Another1000 ordinary interior raw resamplings matched the
frozen implementation exactly. Native controls verify integer interpolation, DC
ripple/normalization, negative lobes, complete input/quota guards, finite-range
failures and ownership. The complete ten-report batch passed77 native CTest
cases,39 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan cases,106 compiled/executed public
examples,479/479 scoped definitions and ten representative clangd hovers. All4
complete report programs executed and all4 native figures were visually
reviewed. HTML/Markdown computed result and identical source/build/export figure
bytes passed verification. Repeatable receipts are retained under
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-194-203/`.

> References

C. E. Duchon(1979),
[Lanczos Filtering in One and Two Dimensions|https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/apme/18/8/1520-0450_1979_018_1016_lfioat_2_0_co_2.xml],
Journal of Applied Meteorology18(8),1016–1022. Native finite reconstruction
support, border clamping, exact integer zeros and optional actual-weight
normalization are stated separately from general filtering-quality claims.
